data.mobile-app#Mobile App:
We assume that you have set up development environment to build React Native on your machine/server. The Mobile source is located under the metafox-mobile folder.Navigate to folder metafox at metafox-mobile/packages/metafox and create a new folder for Notes app named note.Notes app should contain the structure as below:
    metafox-mobile/
        packages/
            metafox/
              note/
                src/
                  components/
                  screens/
                  reducers/
                  sagas/
                  constants.ts
                  index.ts
                  layouts.flatten.json
                  layouts.json
                  module.d.ts
                  reducers.ts
                  sagas.ts
                  types.ts
                package.json
                tsconfig.json
Next, we will declare this app name in apps/settings.json.Now, we will add a new screen for Notes app. On this screen, we will simply show the text "This is note home screen" for now.Let's create a new file at metafox-mobile/packages/metafox/note/src/screens/HomeScreen.tsx and add following code:
/**
 * @type: route
 * name: note.home
 * path: /note, /note/:tab(viewAll)
 */
import React from 'react';
import { View, Text } from 'react-native';
function HomeScreen() {
  return (
    <View>
      <Text>This is note home screen</Text>
    </View>
  );
}
export default HomeScreen;
Now, we will open terminal and run following commands to build the mobile app:
yarn config-app
yarn android # OR yarn ios
yarn start
After that, you will need to run mobile app using Android Studio or XCode. Once the app starts, you can navigate to note home screen as follows:
const SomeComponent = () => {
  const { navigationBackend } = useGlobal();
  navigationBackend.navigate('note.home');
// OR
// navigationBackend.push('note.home');
// OR
// navigationBackend.openLink('/note');

  ...
}

